<http://data.silknow.org/event/1c7a9d41-509f-3b07-9e72-35906d9edd54>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This silk fragment was used for bed-hanging and window-curtains at Osterley Park House (OPH 314 to 314F-1949). The bed on which these hangings were used was designed by Robert Adam on 10 April 1779. The room was known as the Yellow Taffeta Bedchamber."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9519763e-532b-36a1-9390-1d64b59151e8> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This silk fragment was used for bed-hanging and window-curtains at Osterley Park House (OPH 314 to 314F-1949). The bed on which these hangings were used was designed by Robert Adam on 10 April 1779. The room was known as the Yellow Taffeta Bedchamber."@en .

